IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ndis-access`

-- National Disability Insurance Scheme Act 2013 (Cth), ss 9, 18-30, 100 -- becoming and ceasing to be a participant -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case. The NDIS (Becoming a Participant) Rules 2016 are not deposited: what they prescribe is an input.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_national-disability-insurance-scheme-act-2013_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Scenario facts (Jake, k092): born 30 August 2006 at KEMH, an Australian citizen by birth, living in Perth; a stroke on
-- 14 March 2063; NDIS access asked for on 15 May 2063, at 56. His 65th birthday is 30 August 2071. Which activities the stroke
-- affects (mobility and self-care), that it is permanent, the day the CEO decides (1 August 2063), any aged care and the
-- review dates are ASSUMED or HYPOTHETICAL. The Social Security Act baseline qualifies him for the disability support pension
-- on 20 points; nothing in ss 21-25 reads the pension, so receiving it neither helps nor hinders access (INFERENCE).

