§ `s 22 -- the age requirements`

-- k092: Jake asks at 56. Under 65 means the request must be made before the 65th birthday.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the age requirements` 20060830 20630515
#ASSERT `Do I meet the age requirements` 20060830 20710829
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the age requirements` 20060830 20710830)

§ `s 23; s 9 -- the residence requirements`

-- k092: Jake, a citizen living in Perth. A New Zealander qualifies only as a protected SCV holder.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirements` `Jake, a citizen living in Perth`
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the residence requirements` `Jake, had he moved overseas`)
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirements` `a New Zealander here on 26 February 2001`
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the residence requirements` `a New Zealander who first came in 2010`)
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirements` `a New Zealander with 14 months here before 2001 who came back`

#ASSERT `Am I a protected SCV holder` `a New Zealander here on 26 February 2001`
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a protected SCV holder` `a New Zealander who first came in 2010`)
#ASSERT `Am I a protected SCV holder` `a New Zealander with 14 months here before 2001 who came back`

§ `s 24 -- the disability requirements`

-- k092: the stroke leaves a permanent neurological and physical impairment; episodic impairments count only if the CEO takes them as permanent.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the disability requirements` `Jake after the stroke`
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the disability requirements` `Jake, had he been expected to recover`)
#ASSERT `Do I meet the disability requirements` `an episodic psychosocial impairment the CEO takes as permanent`
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the disability requirements` `an episodic psychosocial impairment the CEO does not take as permanent`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the disability requirements` `a permanent impairment that substantially reduces no activity`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the disability requirements` `no impairment`)

§ `s 25; s 9 -- early intervention`

#ASSERT `Do I have developmental delay` `a 4-year-old with developmental delay`
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have developmental delay` `a 7-year-old with the same delay`)

#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the early intervention requirements` `Jake after the stroke` `Jake at 56, no developmental delay` `the CEO not satisfied of early intervention`)
#ASSERT `Do I meet the early intervention requirements` `Jake after the stroke` `Jake at 56, no developmental delay` `the CEO satisfied of early intervention`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the early intervention requirements` `a permanent impairment that substantially reduces no activity` `Jake at 56, no developmental delay` `a prescribed impairment whose supports are NDIS supports`
#ASSERT `Do I meet the early intervention requirements` `no impairment` `a 4-year-old with developmental delay` `the CEO satisfied of early intervention`

