§ `ss 29, 29A, 30 -- turning 65, aged care, withdrawal, revocation`

-- k092 onwards: turning 65 does not end Jake's participation; permanent aged care first begun at or after 65 does, unless under
-- a specialist aged care program; permanent aged care begun before 65 does not. Consistent with the Social Security Act baseline,
-- where the DSP gives way only when another pension becomes payable, not on a birthday.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I ceased to be a participant` `Jake turning 65 in August 2071`)
#ASSERT `Have I ceased to be a participant` `Jake entering permanent residential aged care at 70`
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I ceased to be a participant` `Jake, had he entered permanent aged care at 60`)
#ASSERT `Have I ceased to be a participant` `Jake entering permanent aged care on his 65th birthday`
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I ceased to be a participant` `Jake in permanent aged care at 70 under a specialist aged care program`)
#ASSERT `Have I ceased to be a participant` `Jake's death in April 2079`

#ASSERT `Does aged care end my participation` `Jake entering permanent aged care on his 65th birthday`
#ASSERT NOT (`Does aged care end my participation` `Jake in permanent aged care at 70 under a specialist aged care program`)

#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be paid for the support` 20761015 20761001)
#ASSERT `Can I be paid for the support` 20760915 20761001

#ASSERT `What is the shortest cooling-off period` EQUALS 90

#ASSERT `Am I taken to have withdrawn` 91 90 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I taken to have withdrawn` 91 90 TRUE)
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have withdrawn` 91 60 FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`May my participant status be revoked` `Jake at 66, nothing changed but his age`)
#ASSERT `May my participant status be revoked` `a participant who has moved overseas for good`
#ASSERT `May my participant status be revoked` `a participant who did not answer a s 30(3) request`
#ASSERT NOT (`May my participant status be revoked` `a participant who did not answer, for a reason the CEO accepts`)

